From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t20: use the vb2 buffer fields in the frame-channel prepare

The driver's frame_channel_video_buffer.v4l2_buf copy is kzalloc'ed and
never filled.  prepare therefore saw memory=0, fell into the "memory is
invalid" branch and returned -EINVAL, so OpenIMP could not queue one
USERPTR buffer:

    [KernelIF] QBUF failed: idx=0 phys=0x6a00000 len=3133440 err=Invalid argument

vb2 keeps the QBUF metadata in struct vb2_buffer on 7.x.  Copy index,
memory and plane length from there at prepare time.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/driver/t20/sdk/source/tx-isp-frame-channel.c
+++ b/driver/t20/sdk/source/tx-isp-frame-channel.c
@@ -137,6 +137,11 @@
 	void * addr = NULL;
 	int ret = ISP_SUCCESS;
 
+	/* vb2 keeps the QBUF metadata in vb; our copy is stale. */
+	buf->v4l2_buf.index = vb->index;
+	buf->v4l2_buf.memory = vb->memory;
+	buf->v4l2_buf.length = vb2_plane_size(vb, 0);
+
 	/* 目前是单plane操作 */
 	if (vb2_plane_size(vb, 0) < size) {
 		ISP_PRINT(ISP_ERROR_LEVEL,"Data will not fit into plane (%lu < %lu)\n",
